      "source": "model",
      "thought": "Dragapult is at -2 SpA with Focus Sash intact. Kingambit has Supreme Overlord at 1 faint. Plan: U-turn to bring Garchomp in, then Mega Garchomp uses Earthquake, which is super effective on Kingambit. Gholdengo handles Corviknight, Incineroar and Dragapult, so keep it back. Watch for Sucker Punch and Kowtow Cleave.",
      "hidden_reasoning": "I'm noting Kingambit gets a 10% boost from Supreme Overlord with one ally fainted, likely running Kowtow Cleave, Sucker Punch, Iron Head, or Swords Dance. With Dragapult at -2 SpA, its Flamethrower damage against Kingambit would be super effective but significantly weakened, so I'm weighing whether that's still enough given Kingambit's bulk.\n\nRunning the numbers, Flamethrower only chips around 28% of Kingambit's health, which is too weak to be reliable. I'm thinking Garchomp is a much better answer since its Earthquake is super effective on Kingambit's Steel typing and Garchomp outspeeds it, while Gholdengo's moves don't hit Kingambit hard. If Dragapult uses U-turn instead, Bug-type damage is resisted by Steel, but it lets Garchomp switch in safely without taking a hit first.\n\n",
